      "note": [
        "Commenced higher education programmes within 1, 3, 5, 10 years \r\n Refers to registration in higher education programmes. This does not necessarily mean that the person has also started to study. \r\n The statistics in this survey are presented net. This means that, for each individual, only one registration at a university or institute of higher education is counted. \r\n Eligibility from upper secondary school  All upper secondary school graduates automatically have basic eligibility for an institute of higher vocational education. All graduates from preparatory programmes for post-secondary education automatically have basic eligibility for an institute of higher education. Graduates from vocational programmes can add subjects to obtain basic eligibility for an institute of higher education. \r\n Grade point average from upper secondary school  Students who have studied in the International Baccalaureate programme do not obtain course grades on the same scale as students who have studied in other programmes, and are thus not included in the presentation according to grade points. \r\n Level of educational attainment of the parent(s)  Information on the parents’ level of education is obtained from the Register on educational attainment of the population. Information of the parents’ level of education is obtained, if possible, when the pupil was 12 years old. If data is available for both parents, the parent with the highest level of education is selected. \r\n To prevent disclosure of information, random rounding off was applied in the tables.  Cell values 1 and 2 have been rounded off to either 0 or 3 with predetermined probabilities. This is why the study domains sometimes do not add up to the total. ",
        "Data not available = (..) ",
        "Correction 2024-11-20: Statistics reported by national background (Country of birth, approximate and Swedish/foreign background) regarding school leavers, academic year 2022/2023."
